
  <sn><md>### Exogenic Cycle

An **exogenic cycle** is the `movement and transformation` of elements or materials between the **Earth's surface and the atmosphere, hydrosphere, biosphere, and upper lithosphere** through processes operating mainly at or near the Earth's surface.

The term **exogenic** means "originating or occurring outside the Earth's interior."

![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-emon/QDoc/main/SES3/Soil%20and%20Enviromental%20Chemistry/02.Matter%20and%20Cycles%20of%20Matter/assets/exogenic-cyclle.jpeg)

</md></sn>
